From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP: keep static station PSKs separate from the WPS file owner

A generated union of a configured PSK file and static station rows is not the
persistent owner of WPS appends: regeneration and reboot discard learned keys.
Keep the configured primary as the native read/append owner and accept static
station rows through one supplemental read-only input. Read primary then static
to preserve existing row precedence, and swap both inputs for files-only reload.

Reload both inputs transactionally and retain configured raw shared keys.
Common WPS exports select a group key instead of another station's list head;
static-only authentication remains valid without inventing a shared credential.
Synchronize the canonical primary parent before success since setup may create
its target through a symlink. Keep live WPS capability changes synchronized with
native EAP-WSC consumers, shared authentication owners and beacon publication.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

